Z||000016||ChopTop||12-04-2001||01:29 PM||||The Detroit Free Press reported three people claiming to be American citizens who fought with the Taliban are under the control of US/Allied forces.  John Walker 20, is receiving medical attention.  The two others are unidentified and are being held by the United Front.  It has not been determined by US sources if Walker is being considered a prisoner of war or would be returned to the United States.  Walker was identified by his parents who said their son embraced Islam when he was 16, and traveled to Pakistan two years later to study the Koran.  He kept in regular contact with his parents until six months ago.  His parents did not know their son had joined the Taliban forces.  Walker told CNN this his heart had drawn him to the hardline Islamic movement.  “I was a student in Pakistan studying Islam and came into contact with many people connected with Taliban,”, as reported to CNN.||||reg||1
